<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Wal-Mart upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Wal-Mart upgraded.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities said Monday it upgraded Wal-Mart Stores Inc to long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- Cited overseas acquisition potential as reason for upgrade.</p>
<p>-- Raised 1998 earnings estimate to $1.74 per share from $1.72 to reflect higher earnings from international division.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Our conversations with management, coupled with evidence of increased aggression overseas with the acquisition of its Mexican joint venture partner Cifra, lead us to believe more acquisitions may be in the works in Latin America and the Pacific,&quot; analyst Mark Husson said in a research note.</p>
<p>-- Shares fell 1/16 to 34-15/16.</p>
